00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.190
I talk further about the major highlights.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:17.110
As they imposed restrictions on the social
gathering, the group size used to be between

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.890
5-10 people, and they have eliminated it.

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.530
They have reduced physical distancing.

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:28.630
All other restrictions on social gatherings
have also been eased.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:35.659
You had to download the trace-together app
onto your phone before traveling.

00:01:35.659 --> 00:01:36.659
ok?.

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:38.760
it was a part of the pre-departure traveling
requirement.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:46.280
Most likely, the Trace together app is not
needed, except for a few or limited places.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:53.869
But, they could eliminate the trace-together
app since it will not be used in all the venue

00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:57.320
and they have cleared it in a press statement.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:03.210
Further, I want to talk about the people who
are non-Malaysian work permit holders.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.210
ok?

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:09.590
May 01 onwards, you need not submit the entry
approval, as I said in my previous videos,

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:14.460
you need to get the entry approvals, except
for short-term tourists since the entry approval

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:20.770
was removed for them after eliminating the
VTL.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:31.160
But in this case, you do not need the entry
approval with effect from May 1st.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:35.990
These are the direct guidelines by the Ministry
of Health.

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:44.100
And here what you have to do is to get the
pre-departure covid test done before traveling

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.100
to Singapore.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.910
I am talking about those who are working pass
holders.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:55.020
This includes non-Malaysian work permit holders
holding an in-principle approval in the Construction,

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.830
Marine Shipyard, and Process (CMP) sectors.

